Z||000000||Old Lar||01-26-2001||06:34 PM||||"Smoke Signals" is the montly publication for Pontiac Oakland Club International (POCI).  The lastest issue, February 2001, has a cover shot and story on Illinois's  Lothar Bacher's 87 GT with his 4.6 L 300 hp 32 valve Cadillac Nortstar V-8.  The two year trial and error project required some tweaking for after the first time out with this engine "the front end lifted right up!"  <P>I think this may be only the second Fiero cover shot on "Smoke Signals".  The first was Fran Passuite's modified Indy Pace car.  Maybe the national POCI club is starting to recognize the Fiero as a Pontiac.||||reg||14
Z||000001||2birds||01-26-2001||08:14 PM||||Nice to be noticed, finally.  <BR>As far as Fieros go, High Performance Pontiac is generally useless, too, unless you own an older 60's Pontiac or a Camaro-clone F-body.  Interesting enough to read, but not worth buying at the book store for me.||||reg||1
